From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:09:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 460/488] [DS4.1] The image span and its merge by TileLang row
 copies

The span builder's four masked assignments (each a device sync) and its
three casts become two TileLang row copies: the delimiter rows gathered
from a BF16 table stacked once after loading, then the aligner rows
scattered over the IMAGE slots. The processor keeps the span roles on the
host, so the slots need no sync. The merge into the text embeddings
scatters each span at the runner's host mask's slots instead of torch's
index_put of the flattened spans.
